   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] Different random effects results with Stan vs. with MCMChregress or lmer",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Hi—have you tried testing this with fake data simulated from the model?  That way you have a gold standard (the true parameter values) so you’re not just comparing different routines against each other.<div>A</div><div><br><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Apr 7, 2015, at 7:05 PM, Fabricio Vasselai &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">fabricio...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br><div>Dear Stan community,</div><div><br></div><div>I am getting fairly different results for the random effects of my hierarchical models when I estimate these models with Stan in comparison to when I estimate them with R functions such as MCMChregress or lmer.</div><div><br></div><div>I have tried my best to find why my specification in Stan yields different results, but with no success. Therefore, I came ask for your help. To make things clearer, I reviewed my code in light of recent discussions I&#39;ve found here in the list and I also send a chunk of the data (the data can be directly load in R with the &quot;load&quot; R function, which will create the object &quot;db&quot;, which stands for database). I also send the R code which contains my call for MCMChregress and lmer, as well as the model and call for Stan. In the end, it also summarizes the sampled posterior mean of the X1 random effects across 2nd level units. Here it goes:</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\">################################</span><span><br></span><div><span style=\"color:#800\">##### beginning of the code ####</span><span><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">################################</span><span><br><br>load</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;C:/mypath/db.saved&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#data attached in this message</span><span><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">require</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;lme4&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">require</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;MCMCpack&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">require</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;rstan&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#### lmer model ####</span><span><br>m</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>lmer </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> lmer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span> x1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span> x2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span> x1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span> x2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span> L2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>db</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> na</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>action</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;na.exclude&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">View</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>ranef</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>m</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>lmer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span>$L2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#### MCMChregress model ####</span><span><br>m</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>mcmch </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">MCMChregress</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">fixed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span> x1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span> x2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span><br> random</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=~</span><span>x1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span>x2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;L2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span><br> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>db</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> burnin</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> mcmc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> thin</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span>verbose</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span><br> seed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>NA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>start</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> sigma2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>start</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span><br> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Vb</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>start</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> mubeta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Vbeta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.0E6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span><br> r</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> R</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>diag</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)),</span><span> nu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.001</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> delta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.001</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span><br>m</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>mcmch</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>res </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> cbind</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>m</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>mcmch$mcmc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span>$statistics</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span><br> summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>m</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>mcmch$mcmc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span>$quantile</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">View</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>m</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>mcmch</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>res</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#### Stan model ####</span><span><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">require</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;rstan&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span><br><br>db</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>stan </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;y&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>db$y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span><br> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;x1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>db$x1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span><br> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;x2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>db$x2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span><br> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;L2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>db$L2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span><br> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;N&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>nrow</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>db</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span><br> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;G&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>length</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>unique</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>db$L2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)),</span><span><br> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;W&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span>diag</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span><br><br>m</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>stan </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39; <br>data {<br>int&lt;lower=1&gt; N;<br>int&lt;lower=1&gt; G;<br>real y[N];<br>real x1[N];<br>real x2[N];<br>matrix[3,3] W;<br>int L2[N];<br>}<br><br>parameters {<br>real&lt;lower=0&gt; sigma_y;<br>vector[G] a;<br>vector[G] b1;<br>vector[G] b2;<br>real mu_a;<br>real mu_b1;<br>real mu_b2;<br>real&lt;lower=0&gt; tau_a;<br>real&lt;lower=0&gt; tau_b1;<br>real&lt;lower=0&gt; tau_b2;<br>vector[3] B_raw_temp;<br>corr_matrix[3] Tau_b_raw;<br>}<br><br>model {<br>matrix[G,3] B_raw_hat;<br>matrix[3,3] Sigma_b_raw;<br>matrix[G,3] B_raw;<br><br>mu_a ~ normal(0, 100);<br>mu_b1 ~ normal(0, 100);<br>mu_b2 ~ normal(0, 100);<br>tau_a ~ cauchy(0,2.5);<br>tau_b1 ~ cauchy(0,2.5);<br>tau_b2 ~ cauchy(0,2.5);<br><br>Tau_b_raw ~ wishart(3, W);<br>Sigma_b_raw &lt;- inverse(Tau_b_raw);<br><br>for (l in 1:G) {<br>B_raw_hat[l,1] &lt;- mu_a;<br>B_raw_hat[l,2] &lt;- mu_b1;<br>B_raw_hat[l,3] &lt;- mu_b2;<br>B_raw_temp ~ multi_normal(transpose(row(B_raw_hat,l)), Sigma_b_raw);<br>B_raw[l,1] &lt;- B_raw_temp[1];<br>B_raw[l,2] &lt;- B_raw_temp[2];<br>B_raw[l,3] &lt;- B_raw_temp[3];<br>a[l] ~ normal(B_raw[l,1], tau_a);<br>b1[l] ~ normal(B_raw[l,2], tau_b1);<br>b2[l] ~ normal(B_raw[l,3], tau_b2);<br>}<br><br><br>sigma_y ~ cauchy(0,2.5);<br><br><br>for (n in 1:N)<br>y[n] ~ normal(a[L2[n]] + b1[L2[n]]*x1[n] + b2[L2[n]]*x2[n], sigma_y);<br><br><br>}<br>&#39;</span><span><br><br>fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>stan </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span> stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>model_code </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> m</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span><br> data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> db</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span> <br> iter </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">5000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span><br> chains </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span><br> init</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;random&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span><br> thin</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span><br>fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>stan</span><span><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#### Summary of the sampled mean of x1 random effects ####</span><span><br> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#with lmer:</span><span><br> summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>ranef</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>m</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>lmer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span>$L2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span>$x1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span><br> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#with MCMChregress:</span><span><br> summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>m</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>mcmch</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>res</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span>grep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;b.x1.&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span>rownames</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>m</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>mcmch</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>res</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)),</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Mean&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span><br> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#with Stan:</span><span><br> summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>unlist</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>lapply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>extract</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span>fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span>stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span>$b1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span>mean</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">################################</span><span><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">######## end of the code #######</span><span><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">################################</span></div></code></div><br><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>You all will notice that it is a fairly simplified model, so the debug can be made easier. Still, it is a model with a Wishart prior on the covariance between random effects, trying to make it comparable to how MCMChregress works.</div><div><br></div><div>I will be glad to receive any suggestions you might have on why the random effects are so different in my Stan model.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks in advance for your attention and sorry if I am overlooking any obvious detail here.</div><div><br></div><div>Fabricio Vasselai</div><div>University of São Paulo</div></div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Stan users mailing list&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">stan-users+...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792464917283000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2rKr61hrO1wsILKeMnrCNG\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n<span>&lt;db.saved&gt;</span></div></blockquote></div><br></div></div>"
    ]
